Sval: context menu items name the keys that run the same command

A menu item teaches its shortcut by naming the <key> that runs the same
command: MozMenuItem draws it as acceltext, nsMenuItemX as a macOS native
menu's key equivalent, and XULMenuitemAccessible exposes it. Firefox's page
menu, its text field menus and its Places menu name none, so these items
name the keys of browser-sets.inc.xhtml and editMenuKeys.inc.xhtml. The
text field menus open in dialogs that have no edit keys, and
MozMenuItem._computeAccelTextFromKeyIfNeeded logs an error for a key it
cannot find, so they name a key only where their document has it. Back, Forward, Reload and Stop
name theirs only on macOS, where they are text items; elsewhere they are
icons whose tooltips name the key.

